<title>KYRGYZSTAN: Kyrgyz cent bank discount rate up to 49 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Kyrgyz cent bank discount rate up to 49 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BISHKEK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average discount rate of Kyrgyzstan's National (central) Bank rose in February to 49.03 percent annual from 46.65 percent in January, the bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The central bank stopped holding regular credit funds auctions last month and its official discount rate is pegged to a monthly average of yields on three- and six-month Treasury bills.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
